    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1978-p9.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Because \\(x-1\\lt0,\\) \\(\\sqrt{(x-1)^2}=|x-1|=1-x.\\) Therefore \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\left|x-(1-x)\\right|&=|2x-1|\\\\ &=1-2x, \\end{aligned} \\] since \\(2x-1\\lt0.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Use \\(\\sqrt{u^2}=|u|\\)",
        "When \\(x\\lt0,\\) determine the signs of \\(x-1\\) and \\(2x-1\\)"
      ],
